   "styles": [
    {
     "id": "scalar-notebook-1",
     "game": "scalar",
     "version": 1,
     "summary": "Field notebook on a graph-paper desk: paper #FAFAF9, charcoal #18181B ink, teal #14B8A6 accent, thermal green #22C55E / orange #F97316. Fraunces 900 headlines and clue text, Geist Mono labels and numbers. Sharp-cornered white index cards (3 px ink border, hard 8 px offset shadow, orange header rule, teal number tab) are dealt in from off-frame with a decelerating slide-and-settle; a tally card counts the countries that still fit (195 → … → 1) on an honest zero-based bar. Reveal = a speckled green rubber stamp slammed onto the pile, then a ruled locator card (orthographic, answer in teal, neighbours paper with ink outlines). Candidate checklists tick/cross per clue with thermal green/orange marks."
    },
    {
     "id": "continuum-poster-1",
     "game": "continuum",
     "version": 1,
     "summary": "Swiss data poster: cream #F7F3EC paper with a faint 90 px print grid and a pink/black spine bleeding off the left edge; black #111 type and 3–6 px rules, one hot-pink #F472B6 accent used as fills (with black text) for the subject and the answer. Montserrat 900 headlines, Montserrat 600–800 copy, IBM Plex Mono 700 figures. Head-to-head: two stacked white A/B cards with identical hatched empty tracks; at the reveal both bars grow together from one labelled zero line on one linear scale (axis 0 → nice round max), values count up to the exact text, winner turns pink with a check. Missing-slot: an ordinal ladder (equal rungs, “rank order · not to scale”) of two anchors with three dashed A/B/C insertion gaps; the pink target card drops into its gap on the downbeat, then values count up and thin bars grow from the ladder’s left edge, which becomes a labelled zero line. Ease-out entries ≤ 0.5 s, no camera moves, calm think window, source line always visible."
    },
    {
     "id": "whenabouts-almanac-1",
     "game": "whenabouts",
     "version": 1,
     "summary": "Almanac: parchment #F4ECD8 with a soft vignette, laid-paper lines and a double-rule page frame; sepia ink #2B1D0E; highlighter yellow #EAB308 as fill only, deep ochre #A16207 for accent text. Fraunces italic 900 headlines, Geist Mono for years and labels. Typographic event card (double rule, vector fleurons, no photos). A horizontal ruler timeline pans in unlabelled, then carries the A/B/C year marks (or the pinned anchor). Calm ease-out entries; anticipation wind-up; the reveal is a year odometer rolling to the answer (or the “?” token gliding onto its side of the anchor at an honest distance), followed by a single pan/zoom of the ruler and a yellow highlight on the correct mark."
    },
    {
     "id": "tectonic-ocean-1",
     "game": "tectonic",
     "version": 1,
     "summary": "Low-poly ocean: deep navy #0B1F33 full-frame depth gradient with a faint static triangular facet mesh; maps sit in a rounded card of lighter shallow-water navy. Neighbors are muted sand #E8D5B0, other land is dim slate #4A5966 and unlabelled, the answer is warm orange #F2A154 with a subtle low-poly facet overlay. Nunito 900 for the question, 800 for map labels (white with navy halo). Canonical globe rings in one orthographic projection centred on the target, cropped to the generator window. Neighbors drift in radially (0.5 s ease-out); the gap is a dashed white outline pulsing softly; before the reveal a shadow gathers, then the answer piece drops in with a spring and a soft drop shadow, the label pops, and the camera pulls back (span ×2.2, same centre, ease-in-out)."
    }
   ],
